  "notes": "Four bullets, four steps, but not one-to-one: bullet 3 only tells you where to go and bullet 4 carries two separate trades, so bullet 3 merges forward into the river trade and bullet 4 splits into that trade and the return to Miageau. The 10 gil for the waterskin is a cost, not an inventory requirement: gil does resolve as an item, but putting it in items would make Nouveil's step read 'ready to hand in' permanently, for every character, so it stays a note -- the same treatment the corpus already gives the 5,000 gil coffer key in Under Oath. The Cheval River is a genuine markable target and the page says so in as many words ('find a target named the Cheval River'), which is what makes step 3 worth a marker at all. Nouveil gets no grid because the page gives none, only 'nearby Miageau'.",
